cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this task library, please cite it as below and cite the original papers and repositories each task links to."
type: dataset
title: "Autoresearch Tasks: a source-traceable task library from the Human Harness Corpus and SCiEL"
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-09-19
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Turganov
    given-names: Imran
    email: turganovimrun@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A uniform, source-traceable inventory of 1,138 task packages for LLM-driven
  program, prompt and agent evolution: 1,033 named task packages from the 98
  systems of the Human Harness Corpus, 93 packages from the SCiEL project
  (71 mathematical, optimization and AlgoTune examples plus 22 benchmark
  examples), and 12 portable reference tasks. Every package carries a
  machine-readable manifest, pinned source revisions or archive checksums,
  explicit implementation status, prerequisites, limitations and, where
  established, a direct candidate evaluator adapter and recorded execution
  evidence. The library exposes one facade for discovery, setup, evaluation
  and seed checks through the SCiEL evolutionary engine.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - evolutionary search
  - program synthesis
  - AlphaEvolve
  - OpenEvolve
  - SCiEL
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: website
    title: "Someone Wrote the Evaluator: Human Input in Self-Improving LLM Harnesses (Human Harness Corpus)"
    url: https://human-harness-corpus.small-pine-3af7.workers.dev/
    date-accessed: 2026-09-19
  - type: software
    title: "SCiEL: Scientific Closed-loop Evolutionary Learning"
    url: https://github.com/luciferkonn/SCiEL
    version: da80706f98f9bf1295e502544cdf5a9200fe5f57
    license: Apache-2.0
  - type: software
